A||||2||cscougar||Another idle problem||||1||
Z||000000||cscougar||05-29-2001||12:27 PM||||My 85 v-6 is surging at idle...800 to 1000 rpm.. It also has started dying while going down the road.  It will restart immediately but this is annoying.  It starts this after warming up usually.  <P>I have replaced the TPS, EGR, Coil and disconnected the TCC solenoid.  I have sprayed WD40 to try to find vacuum leaks and haven't found any.<P>Any one have an idea.  It is like a miss but intermittent||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||05-29-2001||01:26 PM||||Have you checked the EGR tube for cracks?  That is usually the biggest source of vac leaks in V6's.<P>The dying while going down the road when warmed up sounds like the ignition module is acting up.  If it hasnt been replaced recently, it should.  Some V6 owners even keep a spare ignition module becuase of their propensity to be fried from the heat.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||Devotshka||05-29-2001||06:08 PM||||I agree with FieroJoe totally.... i once bought an aftermarket ignition module and within about one month it went bad and did exactly that.  Had a tendency to cut out at freeway speed then magically come back to life.  Needless to say my old module went right back in, and, yes, i keep a spare in the trunk in the event that that module should finally die  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
